  "question": {
    "text": "The length of the second's pendulum on the surface of the earth is <math><mn>1&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. If the acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the moon is one-sixth of the acceleration due to gravity of the earth, then the length of the second's pendulum on the surface of the moon will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6&nbsp;</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>36&nbsp;</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>36&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Seconds pendulum is a special pendulum having a time period of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.<br /><br />Using the formula <math> <mrow> <mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msqrt> <mrow> <mfrac> <mi>L</mi> <mi>g</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math><br /><br />If the time period remains the same and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math> is reduced by a factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>.<br />L should be reduced by a factor of 6.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> on moon."
  }
